# Local demo credentials. The only required variable: DATABASE_URLS (a single URL in this package). Optional: DATABASE_REPLICA_URLS.
# The CLI, tools and integration tests need a direct PostgreSQL URL (session advisory lock). The application process must point the same variable at a
# transaction-mode pooler (e.g. PgBouncer); otherwise db.ready() throws POOLER_REQUIRED (skipped with createDb `pooler: "assumed"`):
# DATABASE_URLS=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5563/app
DATABASE_URLS=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5560/app
# Optional read replicas (plain URL list, at most 8, comma-separated). A malformed value throws INVALID_CONFIG when the config loads.
# DATABASE_REPLICA_URLS=postgres://admin:local_admin_password@127.0.0.1:5566/app
